{"text": "from\n\nTHE AMERICAN MEDICAL ASSOCIATION\n\n535 North Dearborn Street + + + Chicago 10, Illinois + + + Phone: Wilitehall 4- 1500\n\nFor P.M, Release Friday, Dec. 30, 1960\n\nCONTENTS\nHospital's trouble shooting clinic aids \u2018lonely crowd\u2019 - - - - - - ~page\nf>Less TB said to be factor in increasing lung cancer - - page\nAging affects cholesterol-produced atherosclerosis in rabbits- page\nForced retirement seen declining page\n\nres\n\nHOSPITAL'S TROUBLE SHOOTING CLINIC\nAIDS \u2018LONELY CROWD\u2019\n\nCHICAGO--A walk-in around-the-clock clinic for handling\nemotional problems has proved to be a popular service of the hospital\nwhere it was set up as the first of its kind,\n\nThe Trouble Shooting Clinic of the City Hospital at Elmhurst,\nNew York City, created in October 1958, \u201chas been successful in\nfinding acceptance and in serving a useful community function,\u201d\u201d\naccording to the current (Dec. 31) Journal of the American Medical\nAssociation,\n\nA total of 2,000 persons have been treated so far,\n\nThe clinic is part of the general hospital's comprehensive\ncommunity psychiatric program for the prevention and cure of psy-\nchiatric and emotional problems.\n\n\u2018The program includes separate psychiatric seminars for general\npractitioners, chaplains, guidance teachers, and lawyers. A school for\nparents and \u2018a program of annual psychiatric check-ups for children\nare planned in the future.\n\n\u201c'It has been our aim, ,,to reach key community figures. . .with\nthe specific purpose of creating, in our community, an awareness of\npsychiatric problems and a sounder psychodynamic understanding,\u201d\nDr, Leopold Bellak, Larchmont, N.Y., wrote in the Journal,\n\nDr. Bellak, chief instigator of the trouble shooting clinic, termed\nit a place where \u201c\u2018anyone may walk in and simply talk things over.\u201d\n\nSTSsbTto", "words": [{"text": "from", "x0": 306, "y0": 152, "x1": 340, "y1": 171, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "THE"